 ## Proof
 
 `node ux/Dictate/test/settings.mjs <base-url>`: the delay holds across a reload; at 3 s two sentences 1 s apart are one prompt, at 0.5 s they are two; the batch seconds reach `/api/session/settings`; choosing One assistant posts `assistant: "single"`, the live line reads it back from the server, and it holds across a reload (shot `assistants-360.png`). Shots: `ai/sessions/2026/10/20/session-e00f55c9/sessions-and-tasks/dictation-debug/settings/shots/` (`panel-400.png`, `panel-1920.png`).
+
+## Plugin settings per session, and "Make default" (Servex side)
+
+A voice session's plugin switches and values are one plain object, `{Name: {enabled?, config?}}` (only what that session changed; anything missing is the class default). Servex keeps it in the session's record in `sessions.json` as `plugins`: `POST /api/session/settings {session, plugins}` sets it (`null` clears it, which is "Reset to default"), `GET /api/session/<id>` returns it, so a phone and a PC read the same. A new session has none, so it starts from the defaults. The shared defaults ("Make default") are one more object of the same shape in `session-defaults.json` beside `sessions.json`: `POST /api/session/defaults {plugins}` sets it, `GET /api/session/defaults` reads it, and the page will read it at load with `localStorage` as the fallback (not built yet: the Servex side only). Both are checked by `checked_plugins()` in `Servex/agents/Sessions.js` (an object of booleans, numbers and short strings, nothing nested). Tests: `node Servex/agents/Sessions.plugins.test.mjs`. The page side (the Features section, the toggles) follows `core/Plugin`'s per-instance rows.
